 How it works:
 
 - `buildNotificationPlan()` (`src/utils/notifications.ts`) is a pure function: settings + language + meal and custom-button names → a list of daily alarms (`id`, hour, minute, title, body, target screen). IDs are stable: water `1000+`, meals `2000-2004`, custom `3001`, weight `3002`, log `3003`.
-- **Android:** `@capacitor/local-notifications` (v8) schedules each alarm as a repeating *daily* system alarm (`schedule.on = {hour, minute, second: 0}`, `allowWhileIdle`), so reminders arrive with the app closed and are restored after a reboot by the plugin's boot receiver. Three notification channels (*Water reminders*, *Meal reminders*, *Other reminders*, named in the app language) let the user tune sound per type in Android's own settings. The notification icon is `drawable/ic_stat_kak.xml`: the app's **real logo** (the K plus the three-tier poop, same coordinates as `kakcalculator-icon.svg`) as a one-colour glyph on a **transparent background** (no disc). Android only uses the alpha channel, so the system paints it in its own circle on the left of the notification and in the status bar. To keep it recognisable at 20 dp the K is cut away around the poop (the logo's cream halo) and the poop's three tier lines are transparent, so it reads as a swirl and not a blob (an earlier solid version looked like a K next to a triangle). No `largeIcon` is set, so nothing is drawn on the right. Re-generate it with `npm i --no-save paper-jsdom && node scripts/generate-notification-icon.mjs`. The name is protected from resource shrinking in `res/raw/keep.xml`. Android 13+ asks for the `POST_NOTIFICATIONS` permission the first time a reminder is switched on. On Android 12+ without the "alarms & reminders" special access the plugin falls back to inexact alarms, so a reminder may be delayed by a few minutes. `AndroidManifest.xml` repeats `POST_NOTIFICATIONS`, `SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM` and `RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED` so all requirements are visible in one place (the widgets themselves use no exact alarm).
